   "search": "dcps budget transparency portal dcps school-by-school budget allocations under the three-factor model (enrollment / targeted / stability). standalone .com domain, not under dcps.dc.gov — easy to miss. allocation, not expenditure — differs from osse ppe. the consolidated fy initial+submitted spreadsheet is a direct .xlsx; the per-school worksheets and prior years live behind a js 'datasets' browser (dcpsbudget.com/datasets) that's browser-only, not script-fetchable. web portal + downloadable excel spreadsheets finance fy27 initial & submitted budget spreadsheet (school-by-school allocations) fy27 submitted budgets this spreadsheet represents submitted budgets by fund source. these budgets were built off of initial allocations and submitted by school leaders and communities in february 2026. dcps operating budget funds are coded under agency code ga0. non-local funds for school resources including title i, title ii, and title iv-b are coded as gd0 as they are loaded to osse’s budget and not dcps’s. this budget worksheet includes school budgeted items funded under both ga0 (dcps) and gd0 (osse); however, in the mayor's budget book ga0 and gd0 are separated into different sections. fy27 initial allocations this spreadsheet represents fy27 initial allocations for dcps schools. from these initial allocations, school leaders and communities develop submitted budgets. in fy27, dcps is providing allocation fund source as well as the dcps funding model allocation type. fy26 initial, submitted & amended budget spreadsheet (school-by-school) fy26 amended worksheet this spreadsheet represents amended school budgets. in march 2025, school principals submitted their fy26 (sy25-26) budget as part of the proposed dcps agency-wide budget. over the summer as part of a process called summer reprogramming, principals have an opportunity to make changes to their budgets, including adding and adjusting positions or non-personnel items. additionally, eligible schools may apply for and receive over-enrollment budget assistance to budget for additional staff members due to over-enrollment. in fy26, dc council awarded additional schools first in budgeting funds to some schools. the budgets on this page are relfective of changes as of october 2025. fy26 submitted worksheet this spreadsheet represents submitted budgets by fund source. these budgets were built off of initial allocations and submitted by school leaders and communities in march 2025. any one-time budget assistance a school received is included in school submitted budgets. dcps operated funds, at the school- and central-level, are coded under agency code ga0. non-local funds for school resources, like title funding such as title i, title ii, and title iv-b are coded as gd0 because they are ultimately loaded onto osse’s budget and not dcps’s. this budget worksheet includes school budgeted items funded under both ga0 (dcps) and gd0 (osse); however, in the mayor's budget book as found on cfo.dc.gov, school profiles separate school budgeted items under ga0 and gd0 into different sections. fy26 initial allocation this spreadsheet represents fy26 initial allocations for dcps schools. from these initial allocations, school leaders and communities develop submitted budgets. in fy26, dcps is providing allocation fund source as well as the dcps funding model allocation type. fy25 amended, submitted & initial budgets (data download) fy25 initial allocation this spreadsheet represents school initial allocations. from these initial allocations, school leaders and communities developed submitted budgets. these submitted budgets are located on the tab \"fy25 submitted budget\" fy25 submitted budget this spreadsheet represents submitted budgets by fund source. these budgets were built off of initial allocations and submitted by school leaders and communities in february 2024. it has been updated in may 2024 to show alignment to the mayor's submitted budget as displayed in the budget book. fy25 amended long this spreadsheet represents amended school budgets. in march 2024, school principals submitted their fy25 (sy24-25) budget as part of the proposed dcps agency-wide budget. over the summer, principals have an opportunity to make changes to their budgets, a process known as budget reprogramming, including adding and adjusting positions or non-personnel items. additionally, this year, dc council provided additional funding to some schools. the budgets on this page are relfective of changes as of october 2024. fy24 initial, submitted & amended budgets fy24 initial allocations school code school name allocation strategy item name fte amount fy24 submitted budget code school name budgeted item fte total budget 21st century at-risk ell upsff local title i title ii fy24 amended budget code school name budgeted item submitted budget fte/quantity reprogrammed quantity final amended budget fte/quantity final amended cost fy23 initial allocations (three strategies) enrollment based school code school name item name fte amount targeted support school code school name item name fte amount stability school code school name item name fte amount fy23 submitted budgets fy23 submitted budget school name budgted item fte total budget local at risk el upsff title i title ii 21st cc at-risk economically disadvantaged poverty low-income low income free lunch frpl farms disadvantaged title i english learner english language learner el ell esl multilingual limited english finance per-pupil per pupil expenditure spending budget cost funding accountability star school quality sqr pmf aspire rating educators teachers teacher school leaders workforce staffing"
